1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,744
Details that win marks.

2
00:00:01,744 --> 00:00:09,700
In a defining clause you may drop the pronoun when it is the object: this is the book I told you about; but never when it is the subject.

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:14,531
That is preferred after superlatives and after all, only and nothing.

4
00:00:14,531 --> 00:00:20,651
A preposition may go before whom or which, or at the end, but never before that.

5
00:00:20,651 --> 00:00:27,669
And a relative clause can often shrink to a participle: the boy standing at the gate; the letter written by him.

